# {{FRONTEND_DIR}} structure

This is a **blank slot**, not a default pattern — this framework
doesn't assume any particular frontend architecture (feature folders,
a component library facade, a specific state-management approach, or
none of that if the frontend is simple). Write down your project's
actual structure here, precisely enough that `coder` and `reviewer`
can check dependency/boundary violations against it mechanically.
Delete this file (and its row in `CLAUDE.md`'s index) entirely if the
project has no frontend, or no boundaries worth documenting yet.

**How this doc stays true (framework ADR 0019).** It describes the code; it
doesn't prescribe what the code should become. A deviation is never a
pattern to copy: mark it as `> **Pitfall:**`, `> **Convention:**` or
`> **Finding (needs a decision):**`, and give a finding (and any
checkable dependency rule) a census probe. No inventory counts in prose —
counts live in the census. A version derived automatically starts
`status: draft` with a banner; `coder`/`reviewer` treat its rules as
advisory until `/update-docs promote` verifies them against code. See
`docs/workflow/living-architecture-docs.md`.

